WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.336 --> 00:00:01.826
A Utah polygamist family

00:00:01.826 --> 00:00:03.910
the focus of a federal raid today.

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:05.590
This is the work of the Lord.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.144
Utah's Kingston clan or The Order,

00:00:08.144 --> 00:00:11.183
it's also called that, a
breakaway Mormon group.

00:00:11.183 --> 00:00:14.667
The Order isn't really well-known

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.710
if you're not a part of it

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.993
or if you're not in law enforcement

00:00:18.993 --> 00:00:23.499
or if you're not involved
in some type of a

00:00:23.499 --> 00:00:26.610
I guess you could call it
the polygamist underworld.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.968
One of the unique things
about the Kingston clan

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.000
compared to other polygamous groups

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.000
is that they do live right in
the middle of suburban Utah.

00:00:36.558 --> 00:00:41.558
And the way they do this is by
not attracting any attention.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.850
They had something like
a hundred businesses,

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.575
including a casino, a rifle manufacturer

00:00:48.575 --> 00:00:53.575
and the biodiesel fuel plant
that Jacob Kingston set up.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:59.090
Jacob Kingston has three
wives and 20 children.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:00.828
He grew up poor in Utah,

00:01:00.828 --> 00:01:03.105
had sort of a hardscrabble life

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:08.105
and was drawn to a very flashy
businessman from Los Angeles

00:01:08.851 --> 00:01:11.019
who drove fast cars,

00:01:11.019 --> 00:01:15.909
flew around in private jets
and took vacations on yachts.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.908
Jacob Kingston was
seduced by that lifestyle

00:01:18.908 --> 00:01:21.712
and that ultimately led to him

00:01:21.712 --> 00:01:25.173
leading a much fuller life of crime.

00:01:34.095 --> 00:01:35.527
My name is Jesse Hyde.

00:01:35.527 --> 00:01:38.280
I'm a magazine writer based in Utah.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.156
My name is David Voreacos.

00:01:40.156 --> 00:01:43.420
I'm a legal reporter at Bloomberg News.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.560
And we wrote The Polygamous Accused

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.143
of Scamming the U.S. Out of $500 Million.

00:01:50.297 --> 00:01:51.340
Jacob Kingston

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.160
is part of the Davis
County Cooperative Society

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.343
also known as The Order. And in The Order,

00:01:58.343 --> 00:02:02.309
the men are given numbers.
There's a hierarchy,

00:02:02.309 --> 00:02:07.309
and they are expected to tie
their earnings into the church.

00:02:07.746 --> 00:02:12.433
And the leaders of the church
have a very strong hand

00:02:12.433 --> 00:02:16.234
in how they lead their
lives, the choices they make,

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:19.583
the wives they choose, the jobs they hold.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.932
One of their early leaders

00:02:22.932 --> 00:02:25.470
taught a principle that's very common

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:29.200
in Mormon fundamentalism
called "bleeding the beast."

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.182
Because polygamy is illegal in the U.S.,

00:02:34.182 --> 00:02:37.236
there's a belief that
the federal government

00:02:37.236 --> 00:02:39.265
really is the enemy.

00:02:39.265 --> 00:02:42.230
And so with many of these groups,

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:45.330
there's nothing wrong
with figuring out ways

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.977
to quote unquote

00:02:46.977 --> 00:02:49.567
"bleed the beast" or
"fleece the government."

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:52.370
The Kingstons over the
years have been investigated

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:55.540
for tax fraud,

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.155
child-welfare fraud.

00:02:57.155 --> 00:02:59.090
One of the more common things

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:02.510
that former members told me they would do,

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.350
and they were encouraged
to do by their leaders,

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:09.446
is a mother would go in and
claim that she was a single mom

00:03:09.446 --> 00:03:14.446
with seven kids to qualify
for different benefits

00:03:14.495 --> 00:03:15.620
when in fact

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:18.502
she could have been the third
or fourth wife of a husband.

00:03:18.502 --> 00:03:21.890
Over the past few years,
members of the Kingston family

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:25.658
who ran a different company
called Washakie Renewable Energy

00:03:25.658 --> 00:03:29.289
have pleaded guilty to dozens
of charges including fraud,

00:03:29.289 --> 00:03:32.242
money laundering and obstruction.

00:03:32.242 --> 00:03:34.670
Jacob Kingston, from what I understand,

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:37.990
actually had the idea to build

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:41.860
this biodiesel production plant.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.058
He recognized that there
was a huge opportunity.

00:03:44.058 --> 00:03:49.058
The federal government was
really pushing renewable energy,

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.080
alternative fuels,

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.447
and there were big tax
credits you could get.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.968
Prior to Jacob,

00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:02.968
they had sort of focused on
businesses like pawn shops,

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.973
or commercial property
that's kind of shabbier.

00:04:10.076 --> 00:04:13.036
Jacob was taking them into the big leagues

00:04:13.036 --> 00:04:16.921
where he's standing courtside at halftime

00:04:16.921 --> 00:04:20.860
at a Utah Jazz game, presenting
a big check to a charity.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:25.860
So this really was a matter
of moving from the shadows

00:04:25.948 --> 00:04:29.270
into the public arena.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:32.637
You could almost think
of like "The Godfather,"

00:04:32.637 --> 00:04:34.660
or any sort of mafia movie,

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:38.660
where over time, you want to
go into legitimate business.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.823
You don't want to live
in the shadows anymore.

00:04:41.751 --> 00:04:46.238
After Jacob Kingston got
his Ph.D. in engineering,

00:04:46.238 --> 00:04:50.692
he then set up a plant in northern Utah

00:04:50.692 --> 00:04:52.849
on his father's ranch.

00:04:52.849 --> 00:04:56.950
What they did was produce biodiesel fuel,

00:04:56.950 --> 00:05:00.713
which takes animal fat
or used cooking oil,

00:05:00.713 --> 00:05:03.483
and through a chemical process,

00:05:03.483 --> 00:05:08.483
converts it into a type of
fuel that works in trucks

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.666
and in manufacturing facilities.

00:05:11.666 --> 00:05:16.182
The pure version of that
fuel is known as B100.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:21.182
And what they then did
was apply for tax credits

00:05:21.752 --> 00:05:23.282
that are administered

00:05:23.282 --> 00:05:26.060
by both the Environmental
Protection Agency

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.070
and the Internal Revenue Service.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:31.600
Those tax credits were a dollar a gallon

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.283
for the fuel that they produced

00:05:33.283 --> 00:05:37.280
that was B100 or what's called B99,

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:39.061
a slightly diluted version.

00:05:39.061 --> 00:05:41.220
And they also got a credit

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:46.220
for a renewable identification
number or RIN, R-I-N.

00:05:46.687 --> 00:05:49.260
And that was a dollar a gallon as well.

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:51.580
And those are sort of the unique number

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.945
that can be traded between companies.

00:05:54.945 --> 00:05:56.940
Washakie Renewable Energy,

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.480
a proud partner of the Tour of Utah,

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:59.712
is leading the intermountain west

00:05:59.712 --> 00:06:02.810
to a future where our air
is clear, clean and healthy.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:04.796
It did start as a legitimate business.

00:06:04.796 --> 00:06:08.614
Kingston found that he could not compete

00:06:08.614 --> 00:06:11.580
because of the limitations on his location

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.819
and the difficulties in
producing the material.

00:06:14.819 --> 00:06:17.524
So he began to cut corners and cheat

00:06:17.524 --> 00:06:20.463
the way other people in
the industry did as well.

00:06:22.383 --> 00:06:26.842
In 2011, Washakie had
run into some troubles.

00:06:26.842 --> 00:06:31.842
The biodiesel they were
creating called B99

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:33.537
was being rejected.

00:06:33.537 --> 00:06:34.878
It wasn't pure enough.

00:06:34.878 --> 00:06:38.060
And so he was looking
for someone to buy it.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.640
And so he had sent a salesman out

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:43.130
to people who were
involved in this business

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:43.963
who might buy it.

00:06:43.963 --> 00:06:47.160
And that's how he came across Lev Dermen,

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.858
and that was the beginning

00:06:48.858 --> 00:06:53.620
of what initially was a
really profitable enterprise

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:54.470
for both of them.

00:06:57.186 --> 00:07:01.667
Lev Dermen, who called himself The Lion,

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:06.667
was a man who, you could
say, a self-made immigrant

00:07:07.073 --> 00:07:12.073
who created an oil and gas
empire in Southern California.

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:15.149
And in his adult life,

00:07:15.149 --> 00:07:20.149
he was constantly under investigation.

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:24.019
And we talked to one of his associates

00:07:24.019 --> 00:07:28.790
who said that the first time he met Lev,

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:33.790
he was struck by a guy who was
almost like wearing a costume

00:07:34.029 --> 00:07:35.333
of a mobster.

00:07:35.333 --> 00:07:39.333
He was wearing blue alligator
shoes, a blue alligator belt.

00:07:39.333 --> 00:07:42.127
He had an office in Rodeo
Drive, and it was like,

00:07:42.127 --> 00:07:45.923
"Hey, let's go down here for a meal.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:51.330
My chauffeur will take us,
and it's like a block away."

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.910
But hey, if I can get into my Rolls-Royce

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:57.930
and take you a block and
the restaurant shut down

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:58.973
just for me,

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.343
that's going to create this appearance

00:08:02.343 --> 00:08:07.343
that I am like an organized-crime boss.

00:08:07.362 --> 00:08:10.039
And so he sort of
carried himself that way.

00:08:10.039 --> 00:08:13.240
It's a question of how much of
that was just for appearance

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.223
and how much of that was real.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.110
When they first met,

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:21.167
Lev Dermen flew his private jet to Utah

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:24.889
to meet Jacob Kingston and his wife Sally.

00:08:24.889 --> 00:08:29.600
Dermen then flew them to
Seattle to meet a friend of his.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.400
He wined them and dined them.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:34.604
The Kingstons had never
been wined and dined before.

00:08:34.604 --> 00:08:36.582
They'd never been on a private jet.

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:39.300
They went to a seafood store

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:43.363
and Lev Dermen bought the entire contents

00:08:43.363 --> 00:08:47.429
of the seafood store to
bring home for the Kingstons.

00:08:47.429 --> 00:08:51.790
Over time, Jacob Kingston was dazzled

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:55.443
by Lev Dermen's fast-living lifestyle.

00:08:55.443 --> 00:08:58.375
They bought very expensive sports cars

00:08:58.375 --> 00:09:02.849
like a $1.8 million
Bugatti for Lev Dermen.

00:09:02.849 --> 00:09:07.849
They bought a waterfront house
in California for Lev Dermen.

00:09:07.936 --> 00:09:12.320
They bought a $3 million house in Utah

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.440
for Jacob Kingston.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.113
They took trips together.

00:09:16.113 --> 00:09:20.029
He started dressing in a flashier way,

00:09:20.029 --> 00:09:22.110
started wearing cologne.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:24.187
He started cutting his hair differently.

00:09:24.187 --> 00:09:26.160
It really started to change him.

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:31.110
He got a taste for the high
life, and he wanted that.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:33.810
And in pursuing that

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:38.810
he was sort of breaking
an unspoken Order rule,

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.911
and that rule is to not draw attention.

00:09:41.911 --> 00:09:46.911
If you start wearing flashy
suits and driving fancy cars

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:52.300
and having a luxury
suite at Utah Jazz games,

00:09:53.748 --> 00:09:57.840
being public with your company,
sponsoring different things,

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.520
you're going to draw attention.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:03.040
And so Jacob had a dilemma.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:08.040
Do we keep operating the way
my uncles have run the family

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.134
by staying in the shadows?

00:10:11.134 --> 00:10:12.980
Or do we go big?

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:15.310
Do we try to make a lot of money?

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:18.023
And for whatever reason
he chose the latter.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:26.423
The EPA did not enforce
its standards stringently

00:10:26.423 --> 00:10:30.181
and what fraudsters soon learned

00:10:30.181 --> 00:10:33.960
is that if they were able
to produce documentation

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:37.668
that showed that they had
produced biodiesel fuel,

00:10:37.668 --> 00:10:40.610
that the government
accepted that documentation

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.571
and they got their credits.

00:10:42.571 --> 00:10:45.264
Eventually the government
got more sophisticated

00:10:45.264 --> 00:10:48.544
at rooting out the fraudsters,
but there were several years,

00:10:48.544 --> 00:10:51.460
particularly in the early
years, Jacob Kingston

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.081
and Lev Dermen perpetrating their fraud,

00:10:54.081 --> 00:10:57.257
that the government
was not able to keep up

00:10:57.257 --> 00:10:58.683
with the fraudsters.

00:11:00.235 --> 00:11:02.384
So there was one particular fraud

00:11:02.384 --> 00:11:05.150
where the Kingstons and Lev Dermen

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:10.150
used a supplier in Florida and Houston,

00:11:10.201 --> 00:11:14.118
who shipped B99 on a barge and sent it

00:11:14.118 --> 00:11:16.312
to the east coast of Panama,

00:11:16.312 --> 00:11:18.943
and that generated phony paperwork.

00:11:18.943 --> 00:11:23.023
And then they trucked it over
to the west coast of Panama

00:11:23.023 --> 00:11:25.080
and they put it on a different boat

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:28.350
and shipped it up to Los Angeles

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:29.809
where Lev Dermen's company

00:11:29.809 --> 00:11:32.671
said that he was shipping it to Utah

00:11:32.671 --> 00:11:37.260
for processing at Kingston
biodiesel fuel plant,

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:38.483
the Washakie plant.

00:11:39.663 --> 00:11:42.831
I talked to a guy who worked for Jacob

00:11:42.831 --> 00:11:44.438
and he told me that they filled up

00:11:44.438 --> 00:11:46.697
an entire rail car with water.

00:11:46.697 --> 00:11:48.149
As long as they had the documents

00:11:48.149 --> 00:11:51.886
to show that they were moving
what looked like biodiesel,

00:11:51.886 --> 00:11:56.379
the inspections were so laxed
to basically non-existent,

00:11:56.379 --> 00:11:58.651
but that was enough to fool the government

00:11:58.651 --> 00:12:00.443
and cash in on these tax credits.

00:12:02.894 --> 00:12:05.774
The largest and most dramatic example

00:12:05.774 --> 00:12:10.774
where two checks combined
total more than $160 million,

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:13.343
that was ultimately their biggest payday.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.856
There were other claims that they put in

00:12:15.856 --> 00:12:19.353
that were disallowed as the government

00:12:19.353 --> 00:12:23.520
eventually caught on fully to their fraud.

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.422
Jacob Kingston and his
family were arrested

00:12:26.422 --> 00:12:30.190
as they boarded a plane in Salt Lake City

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:31.688
headed for Turkey.

00:12:31.688 --> 00:12:32.997
Anything you'd like to say?

00:12:32.997 --> 00:12:35.830
My client's not gonna have any...

00:12:40.919 --> 00:12:43.241
A lot of the initial questions

00:12:43.241 --> 00:12:47.617
that prosecutors were starting to ask

00:12:47.617 --> 00:12:48.976
kind of tipped their hand

00:12:48.976 --> 00:12:53.261
that this wasn't going to just be a case

00:12:53.261 --> 00:12:55.820
about Washakie Renewable Energy.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:58.019
This was going to be
a case about The Order

00:12:58.019 --> 00:13:00.378
and all of their businesses.

00:13:00.378 --> 00:13:03.800
And this would put everything
they had built at risk.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:08.800
So in a way Jacob took this
big gamble for the family.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:11.786
Let's go big time.

00:13:11.786 --> 00:13:12.983
Let's step out of the shadows.

00:13:12.983 --> 00:13:15.024
Let's make a lot of money.

00:13:15.024 --> 00:13:18.889
And at the end, he paid
the ultimate price.

00:13:18.889 --> 00:13:20.250
Yeah that's right,

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.379
the Kingston Clan has their fingers

00:13:21.379 --> 00:13:22.963
in all kinds of businesses:

00:13:22.963 --> 00:13:25.810
oil lubes, grocery stores,

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:28.657
hardware stores, private-investigator
firms, biodiesel.

00:13:28.657 --> 00:13:31.027
And that biodiesel allegedly helped pay

00:13:31.027 --> 00:13:33.696
for that $4 million mansion in Sandy

00:13:33.696 --> 00:13:35.980
where one of those
warrants was served today.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:38.301
The prosecutors were helped at trial

00:13:38.301 --> 00:13:42.792
by the cooperation of five
people who had pleaded guilty

00:13:42.792 --> 00:13:46.760
and testified under
cooperation agreements.

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.818
They included Jacob Kingston

00:13:48.818 --> 00:13:51.890
and his younger brother, Isaiah.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:55.000
Prosecutors showed at trial that they made

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:59.418
nearly $500 million and
that the claims accelerated

00:13:59.418 --> 00:14:01.536
at the end of the fraud.

00:14:01.536 --> 00:14:06.536
He then sent through a
very complex financial path

00:14:06.559 --> 00:14:09.373
tens of millions of dollars to Lev Dermen.

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:16.843
Now to an eyewitness news investigation

00:14:16.843 --> 00:14:19.670
in the strange alliance
between a suspected mobster

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.482
here in L.A. and a
polygamist clan in Utah.

00:14:22.482 --> 00:14:27.482
Lev Dermen was convicted in March of 2020

00:14:27.904 --> 00:14:32.195
after a six-week trial of
conspiracy money laundering

00:14:32.195 --> 00:14:34.047
and fraud charges.

00:14:34.047 --> 00:14:39.047
Dermen's lawyer complained
that the jurors panicked

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.263
and reached a quick decision

00:14:42.263 --> 00:14:44.773
only because they were
scared about Covid-19

00:14:44.773 --> 00:14:46.676
and they wanted to get out of there.

00:14:46.676 --> 00:14:49.068
I've known my client for decades.

00:14:49.068 --> 00:14:50.963
I'm confident that when he tells me

00:14:50.963 --> 00:14:53.920
that he did nothing wrong
that he's telling the truth.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.665
The second phase of Lev
Dermen's criminal trial

00:14:56.665 --> 00:15:00.213
will be a forfeiture proceeding
that begins later this year,

00:15:00.213 --> 00:15:03.420
in which the government is
trying to recover assets

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.970
that they say were the
product of money laundering.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:10.286
Both Lev Dermen and Jacob Kingston

00:15:10.286 --> 00:15:14.453
are in jail around Salt Lake City.

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.240
Neither has been sentenced.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:20.663
Lev Dermen faces life in prison.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:24.993
Jacob Kingston also faces
many years in prison,

00:15:24.993 --> 00:15:27.423
but as a result of his cooperation

00:15:27.423 --> 00:15:31.382
and the successful
conviction of Lev Dermen,

